{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=u-{e}^{v}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-{e}^{v}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-{e}^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-u,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-v,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{v}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-{e}^{v},\\,-1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨v,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,u⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,-u\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] ["math" "⟨uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩"] ["math" "⟨uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ 1 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,2u-2v⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2u,\\,v+u,\\,2v⟩"] ["math" "⟨u,\\,-2v,\\,u+v⟩"] ["math" "⟨u,\\,u-2v,\\,v⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡u & 0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-105606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] ["math" "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] ["math" "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+1,\\,y={v}^{3}+1,\\,z=2u+v.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}+1,\\,{v}^{3}+1,\\,2u+v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109911" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109911" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-6{v}^{2}+u,\\,-2u+v,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨u-v,\\,2u,\\,{v}^{2}-u⟩"] ["math" "⟨v,\\,-2u,\\,-3u{v}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{v}^{2}-u,\\,2v,\\,u{v}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109911" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 1 \\\\ -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u{sin}^{2}⁡v-6u{cos}^{2}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v)+4{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+40{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡v+8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-105613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+{u}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}+36}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+36}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,3-v,\\,1+4u+5v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+4u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+4u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{u+v}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "u\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 4$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2u}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v),\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2u},\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-{e}^{2u},\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-{e}^{2u})^{2}+({e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+({e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{4u}+{e}^{2u}{sin}^{2}⁡v+{e}^{2u}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{4u}+{e}^{2u}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{4u}+{e}^{2u}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}({e}^{2u}+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\sqrt{{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}"] ["math" "{e}^{2u}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}"] ["math" "{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡v"] ["math" "{e}^{u}\\sqrt{u+1}"] ["math" "{e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 4}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,uv⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 4.$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 2v & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,4uv⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,4uv⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2{v}^{2})^{2}+(-2{u}^{2})^{2}+(4uv)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}+16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}"] ["math" "2u\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+uv}"] ["math" "2{u}^{2}v"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}"] ["math" "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,u-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2v & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2v & 2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,-4uv,\\,-4uv⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2v,\\,-4uv,\\,-4uv⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2v)^{2}+(-4uv)^{2}+(-4uv)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+32{u}^{2}{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}(1+8{u}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{v}^{2}}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{v}^{2}-{u}^{2}}"] ["math" "u\\sqrt{1+4v}"] ["math" "{v}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{u}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105920" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=3u+2,\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105920" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-v,\\,3u+2,\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u+2),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨6,\\,-5,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{70}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105920" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-105920" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105920" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{70}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{30}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{35}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105920" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{70}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-110252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,1-2u+5v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-110252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-2u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-2u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-5,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2,\\,-5,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(-5)}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 2$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 2}\n$$\n\nof radius $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{30}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot (\\sqrt{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-110252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-110252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-110252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi \\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "2\\pi \\sqrt{30}"] ["math" "3\\pi \\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{15}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{20}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-110252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi \\sqrt{30}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=uv,\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $1\\le v\\le 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,uv,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & v & 0 \\\\ 0 & u & v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}v & 0 \\\\ u & v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{v}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,2{u}^{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨{v}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,2{u}^{2}⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({v}^{2})^{2}+(-2uv)^{2}+(2{u}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{u}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({v}^{2}+2{u}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+2{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({v}^{2}+2{u}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({v}^{2}+2{u}^{2})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[u{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{v}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}v]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{2}^{3}+2(2)-({1}^{3}+2(1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(9) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨-u+v,\\,u-2v,\\,3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,3,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4},\n$$\n\nof radius $2.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{19}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi \\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-105922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi \\sqrt{38}"] ["math" "2\\pi \\sqrt{57}"] ["math" "4\\pi \\sqrt{19}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{19}"] ["math" "\\pi \\sqrt{38}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-105922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\pi \\sqrt{19}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y=2-3u,\\,z=1+u-v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $-1\\le v\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,2-3u,\\,1+u-v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2-3u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2-3u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,2,\\,3⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b34876a3aa4f068babb0902ffa93fc00910606c46cdf5801d97070d05574e08c"} {"question" "q-109710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{14}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{22}"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{11}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "q-109710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{22}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7ec705575b1b93b8631c932343a8fb923a3f789f77431c0dc770695acd9e5ff"} {"question" "e-8943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: v^2, \\: u+v \\big\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/example-8943.json" "file_sha256" "282d347fab41ee78f36de79e23bd168bfbf80222bd3c9c6d34831d15ca2d369d"} {"question" "e-8943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2v & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/example-8943.json" "file_sha256" "282d347fab41ee78f36de79e23bd168bfbf80222bd3c9c6d34831d15ca2d369d"} {"question" "e-8958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/assets/95e3f2da04e23c9b42ea04cba3ee1d7cc069fef992592f09a70cef367b670f0d.png)\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: v, \\: u^3-v \\big\\rangle$ for $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 2.$ What is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/example-8958.json" "file_sha256" "044ab0a880bcc97030f9d946b4c6b6ca726ae5ec26872859ec67012d36b14c3b"} {"question" "e-8958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D  \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3{u}^{2},\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-3{u}^{2},\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{u}^{2})^{2}+(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{u}^{4}+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{9{u}^{4}+2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/example-8958.json" "file_sha256" "044ab0a880bcc97030f9d946b4c6b6ca726ae5ec26872859ec67012d36b14c3b"} {"question" "e-8947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx = u, \\quad \ny = v, \\quad \nz = 1 - u - v\n$$\n\nfor $-1 \\leq u \\leq 1$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/example-8947.json" "file_sha256" "0b5e0dfb20e9d3089a60e7068222ddbd7990eac9c5e4bfcf30fe120f72d28be3"} {"question" "e-8947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D  \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u, \\: v, \\: 1 - u - v \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD = \\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq u \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065243/example-8947.json" "file_sha256" "0b5e0dfb20e9d3089a60e7068222ddbd7990eac9c5e4bfcf30fe120f72d28be3"}] "usage" {"q-105613" [] "q-105606" [] "e-8943" [] "e-8947" [] "q-105920" [] "q-109941" [] "q-105922" [] "e-8958" []} "basis" 2138 "retractions" [[17592186119996 :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u, v) = ⟨\\sin u, v^{2}, 4v\\cos u⟩$."] [17592186119998 :question/problem "$∬_(D)AAAAAAAAdA, D = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 1, 0 \\le v \\le π}$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u, v) = ⟨2u\\sin v, 3u\\cos v, u⟩$ for $0 \\le u \\le 1$ and $0 \\le v \\le π$. What is the missing expression?"] [17592186120016 :question/problem "$∬_(D)AAAAAAAAdA, D = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 2, 0 \\le v \\le 2}$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u, v) = ⟨u^{2}, u - v^{2}, v^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le u \\le 2$ and $0 \\le v \\le 2$. What is the missing expression?"] [17592186120003 :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = 2u - v, y = 3u + 2, z = u + 2v$\n\nfor $0 \\le u \\le 1$ and $-1 \\le v \\le 1$."] [17592186120004 :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u, v) = ⟨ - u + v, u - 2v, 3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint $u^{2} + v^{2} \\le 4$."] [17592186120004 :question/answer-fields 17592186116590] [17592186119631 :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: v^2, \\: u+v \\big\\rangle$."] [17592186119631 :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$, the fundamental vector product is defined as $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v$.\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u + v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2u, 0, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u + v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 2v, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2v & 1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2v,-2u, 4uv⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119633 :question/problem "$AAAAAAAA$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: v, \\: u^3-v \\big\\rangle$ for $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 2$. What is the missing expression?"] [17592186119633 :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D$, the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D \\left\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\| \\text{d}A\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{3} - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 0, 3u^{2}⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{3} - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 1,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3u^{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3u^{2} \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3u^{2} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3u^{2}, 1, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}‖ &= ‖⟨ - 3u^{2}, 1, 1⟩‖ \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(3u^{2})^{2} + (1)^{2} + (1)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9u^{4} + 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(S)dS &= ∬_(D)‖r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}‖dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)\\sqrt{9u^{4} + 2}dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119632 :question/problem "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations\n$x = u, \\quad y = v, \\quad z = 1 - u - v$\n\nfor $-1 \\leq u \\leq 1$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 3$."] [17592186119632 :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D$, the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D \\left\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\| \\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u, \\: v, \\: 1 - u - v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(1 - u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 0,-1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′} &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(1 - u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 1,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′} &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 1, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}‖ &= ‖⟨1, 1, 1⟩‖ \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1^{2} + 1^{2} + 1^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 1 + 1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD = \\{(u,v) \\:: \\: -1 \\leq u \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 3\\}\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(S)dS &= ∬_(D)‖r_{u}^{′} \\cdot r_{v}^{′}‖dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)\\sqrt{3}dA \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3}∬_(D)dA \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3} \\cdot Area(D) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3} \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186116543 17592186116544 17592186116545 17592186116546 17592186116547 17592186116555 17592186116556 17592186116557 17592186116558 17592186116559 17592186116585 17592186116586 17592186116587 17592186116588 17592186116589 17592186116591 17592186116592 17592186116593 17592186116594 17592186116662 17592186116663 17592186116664 17592186116665 17592186116666] "immutable_fields" [[17592186116542 :answer-field/correct] [17592186116542 :answer-field/id] [17592186116542 :answer-field/key] [17592186116542 :answer-field/type] [17592186116554 :answer-field/correct] [17592186116554 :answer-field/id] [17592186116554 :answer-field/key] [17592186116554 :answer-field/type] [17592186116584 :answer-field/correct] [17592186116584 :answer-field/id] [17592186116584 :answer-field/key] [17592186116584 :answer-field/type] [17592186116590 :answer-field/correct] [17592186116590 :answer-field/id] [17592186116590 :answer-field/key] [17592186116590 :answer-field/type] [17592186116661 :answer-field/correct] [17592186116661 :answer-field/id] [17592186116661 :answer-field/key] [17592186116661 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
